  <data name="About_Brand_Name" xml:space="preserve"><value>CPFS - CyClone Power File Share</value><comment>Same in every language.</comment></data>
  <data name="About_Brand_Tagline" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your PC's folder, within reach of any device.</value><comment>UNTRANSLATED: English text</comment></data>
  <data name="About_Brand_Description" xml:space="preserve"><value>CPFS shares one folder on a Windows 10 or 11 PC with Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and iOS devices. They connect by the PC's name (ComputerName.local), by its Wi-Fi or LAN address, or by a VPN address, and a phone can connect with a QR code. Sharing is limited to that folder, with a separate account and hardened Windows settings, and the uninstall puts the original settings back. If you run a Linux server, CPFS can also sync one subfolder with it over an encrypted channel. A file deleted or replaced on one side is kept in a versions folder on the other.</value><comment>UNTRANSLATED: English text</comment></data>
